From 63c7a94e736e9535c1f27b8b4e3aefffab043aec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fangjian Ju <roger@FangjiandeMacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:07:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] validate weight-version spans with real
 exceptions and the full writer contract

The 0008 booking guarded the spans with a bare assert that only checked
the first start and contiguity, and the `if spans := meta_info.get(...)`
walrus made an explicit null (or an empty list) fall through to the
scalar fallback as if the engine simply had not reported spans. Both
disguise a corrupt staleness account: asserts vanish under python -O,
and the washed-in fallback books a broken turn as a healthy
single-version one.

- miles/utils/types.py: new _validated_weight_version_spans() enforcing
  the pinned writer contract (sglang weight_versions.py, 4e230c3d) with
  ValueError: a present key must be a non-empty list of
  {version: str, start/end: non-negative int} spans, first start 0,
  contiguous, adjacent versions distinct, the only legal empty span the
  zero-output [v, 0, 0) singleton, and the scalar weight_version present
  and equal to the last span's version. Only a truly absent key falls
  back to the scalar. Numeric versions are rejected, not coerced: the
  writer stringifies explicitly, so a number on the wire is corruption,
  not a dialect. The per-request generated-token count is not among the
  function's inputs, so the end == num-generated coverage check stays
  with the rh2-side parser.
- docs/developer/versions.md: refresh the build-arg table and the
  bumping principle to this tree's actual defaults (SGLANG_IMAGE_TAG
  v0.5.18; SGLANG_COMMIT / MEGATRON_COMMIT pinned since the 0007
  Dockerfile pin, no longer empty).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
